# Documentation Maintenance

When these files — or the code their `globs` / `Primary code` links point at — change, keep documentation current. Prefer the **docs-keeper** agent over ad-hoc rewrites.

## Layers (do not collapse)

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New or renamed domain term | Workspace-root `CONTEXT.md` via `/domain-modeling` |
| Hard-to-reverse architectural decision | `docs/adr/` |
| Service invariants, routing, side-effect order | Matching `.cursor/businesslogic/*.service.md` |
| Folder ownership, process mechanics, auth, env | The `.mdc` whose `globs` already match the path |
| New businesslogic file or rule | `.cursor/index.md` catalog row |

Link glossary terms; do not redefine them. Do not copy owner policy into software-logic rules.

## Glob-scoped rules

- Edit the rule whose frontmatter `globs` match the changed path. If the path moved, fix that rule’s `globs` rather than creating an always-apply duplicate.
- Keep `alwaysApply: true` for maps and safety only (`project-organization`, `codebase`, `backend-safety`).
- One concern per rule. Reference businesslogic docs instead of pasting them.

## Cross-repo

Server behavior stays in `vantage-main-server`. Admin UI maps live in `vantage-admin/.cursor/rules/`. Extension workflows live in `granot_sync_extensions_and_services/.cursor/rules/`. Client-site / `@vantage/api-client` maps live in `vantage-movers-clients/.cursor/rules/`. Cross-link; do not fork the same invariant.

If no documentation update is needed, say so.
